    "narrative": "The LawDog lineup is anchored by **Bryce Harper** (76.31) and **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (73.30), both of whom present as elite daily starts against favorable matchups. **Bryce Harper** draws a prime assignment against Jackson Kent; with an excellent .389 xwOBA and the 5.54 xERA of Kent offering significant upside, he is the clear centerpiece of today\u2019s offense. Similarly, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remains a high-floor, high-ceiling play, benefiting from an advantageous batting order spot and the soft projected ERA of Caleb Murphy. **Cal Raleigh** (68.23) also grades out as a premier catcher play, largely due to the exploitable 5.18 xERA of R. Johnson and a favorable clean-up spot in the order. We are also closely tracking **Jung Hoo Lee** (60.52); while he has a solid base projection, his score is bolstered by a rare \"Slow SP Delivery\" tag, making him a high-efficiency target for stolen bases against Andre Pallante.\n\nPlatoon advantages and volume are the primary drivers for the remainder of the lineup, with **Luis Arraez** (61.72) providing a high-contact floor against the struggling Kent. **Daulton Varsho** (60.09) receives a notable +10% boost from his platoon edge, putting him well ahead of the fringe options. The most difficult decision this morning involved **Gleyber Torres** (50.45), who narrowly missed the starting nine. While **Gleyber Torres** benefits from a strong lineup position, his efficiency metrics against the current rotation were simply outclassed by the platoon-advantaged **Kyle Karros** (58.58), whose +14% park factor boost at his home venue ultimately tipped the scales in his favor. We are benching **JJ Bleday** entirely today, as his sub-40 efficiency score against Yamamoto reflects a high-risk matchup that fails to meet our roster floor requirements, preserving our precious game caps for higher-leverage opportunities later in the week.",
